  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Beyond SOHCAHTOA — the unit circle, inverse trig functions, sum/difference identities, and solving trig equations over a given interval.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Sum formula sin",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\sin(A+B)=\\sin A\\cos B+\\cos A\\sin B \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Sum formula cos",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\cos(A+B)=\\cos A\\cos B-\\sin A\\sin B \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Law of sines",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{a}{\\sin A}=\\dfrac{b}{\\sin B} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Inverse trig",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\sin^{-1},\\cos^{-1},\\tan^{-1} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 4.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Find all solutions to \\( 2\\sin\\theta-1=0 \\) on \\( [0,2\\pi) \\). \\[ \\sin\\theta=\\tfrac{1}{2} \\implies \\theta=\\tfrac{\\pi}{6} \\text{ or } \\theta=\\tfrac{5\\pi}{6}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · Law of Cosines",
          "ar": null
        },
        "canvasId": "act2LawCanvas",
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "A triangle with sides a and b and included angle C, showing the third side c found by the Law of Cosines",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "act2LawDataBtn",
          "panelId": "act2LawDataPanel",
          "descId": "act2LawDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "act2LawDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "The triangle's known sides/angle and the computed third side",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            {
              "en": "quantity",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "value",
              "ar": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "act2LawA",
            "valueDisplayId": "act2LawAlab",
            "label": {
              "en": "side <b>a</b>:",
              "ar": null
            },
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Side a",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": 3,
            "max": 10,
            "value": 7,
            "step": 1
          },
          {
            "id": "act2LawB",
            "valueDisplayId": "act2LawBlab",
            "label": {
              "en": "side <b>b</b>:",
              "ar": null
            },
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Side b",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": 3,
            "max": 10,
            "value": 10,
            "step": 1
          },
          {
            "id": "act2LawC",
            "valueDisplayId": "act2LawClab",
            "label": {
              "en": "included angle <b>C</b>:",
              "ar": null
            },
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Angle C",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": 20,
            "max": 160,
            "value": 60,
            "step": 5
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "act2SideC",
            "label": {
              "en": "c² = a² + b² − 2ab cos C",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "indigo",
            "value": "8.89"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Law of Sines, Cosines & Identities",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<strong>Law of Sines:</strong> \\(\\dfrac{a}{\\sin A} = \\dfrac{b}{\\sin B} = \\dfrac{c}{\\sin C}\\). <strong>Law of Cosines:</strong> \\(c^2 = a^2+b^2-2ab\\cos C\\). Key identities: \\(\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta=1\\); \\(\\sin 2\\theta = 2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta\\); \\(\\cos 2\\theta = \\cos^2\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Law of Cosines",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "A triangle has sides \\(a=7, b=10\\) and included angle \\(C=60°\\). Find side \\(c\\). <p>\\(c^2 = 49 + 100 - 2(7)(10)\\cos 60° = 149 - 70 = 79\\). \\(c = \\sqrt{79} \\approx 8.89\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Prove that \\(\\dfrac{1-\\cos 2\\theta}{\\sin 2\\theta} = \\tan\\theta\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(\\dfrac{1-(1-2\\sin^2\\theta)}{2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta} = \\dfrac{2\\sin^2\\theta}{2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta} = \\dfrac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta} = \\tan\\theta\\). &#10003;",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
